# ChatGPT (Codex) Installation & Setup Guide (English)

[한국어 가이드](./chatgpt.ko.md) · [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest)

One pasted prompt in **Codex (app or CLI)** installs the Claire Bible skills and isolated extractor agent and connects your standalone `claire` MCP server. In **ChatGPT web and desktop**, a read-only custom MCP connector lets you safely search your knowledge graph.

---

## Where Does It Work?

| ChatGPT / Codex surface | What you can do | Where to start |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Codex app**, **Codex CLI** in a terminal | Save, isolated extract, regenerate, and search (`$claire ingest`, `$claire regenerate`, `$claire query`) | Steps 1 to 2 below |
| **ChatGPT web**, **ChatGPT desktop** normal chat | Search (read) only (custom MCP connector, `readonly`) | [Read-only connection](#readonly-connector) at the end |

---

## Before You Start (1 Minute)

1. Sign in to your **Claire Bible web page**. (Extraction mode is chosen per ingest request, so no global mode switch is needed.)
2. Keep **MCP Settings** (`/account/mcp`) open. You copy the **ChatGPT (Codex) quick setup prompt** from this page.

---

## Step 1: Install and Connect via Quick Setup Prompt

1. On the Claire Bible **`/account/mcp`** page, in the **Official Agent Marketplace (GitHub)** card, click **Copy** next to **`ChatGPT (Codex) quick setup prompt`**.
   - To start from GitHub, copy this prompt and replace only `<your-claire-server>` with your server address:
   ```text
   Set up Claire Bible for Codex on this computer.
   1) Download claire-codex-v{{VERSION}}.zip and SHA256SUMS from the latest GitHub Release of
      https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}, verify the checksum, install skills/claire into
      ~/.codex/skills/claire, install agents/claire-extractor.toml into
      ~/.codex/agents/claire-extractor.toml, and append rules/AGENTS.md into ~/.codex/AGENTS.md
      without overwriting existing settings.
   2) Run: codex mcp add claire --url "https://<your-claire-server>/mcp"
   3) Run: codex mcp login claire
   Skip any step already completed, stop and tell me if the codex command is not found,
   and tell me to restart Codex when finished.
   ```
2. Open a new conversation in the **Codex app** or **Codex CLI**, paste the prompt, and send it.
   - *Permission to run commands*: when Codex asks to install files or run `codex mcp add` / `codex mcp login`, allow it.
3. **Claire Bible sign-in (OAuth 2.1)**: `codex mcp login claire` opens your browser. Sign in to Claire Bible and approve the **`readonly`** and **`write`** scopes.
4. Quit and restart the Codex app or CLI.

---

## Step 2: Make Sure It Works

1. Open a new Codex conversation and run `/mcp` to verify that `claire` is connected.
2. Send this prompt to check your knowledge bases:
   ```text
   $claire query Show the list of my knowledge bases
   ```
3. When the answer lists your knowledge base names and document counts, setup is complete.

---

## Three Subcommands Ready to Use (`v{{VERSION}}`)

You only need the unified **`$claire`** skill with three subcommands: **`$claire ingest`**, **`$claire regenerate`**, and **`$claire query`**.

- **`$claire ingest`** (`URL, local file, note, or pending queue`):
  - Stages a web address, local document file (PDF, DOCX, ODT, MD, TXT, RST, ADOC, HTML), or text note on your server and delegates extraction to the isolated `claire-extractor` subagent (`sandbox_mode = "read-only"`).
  - When called with no URL/file/note (or asked to process waiting items), checks `extract_queue` and drains `pending` items staged from the Web UI, Telegram, or feeds.
- **`$claire regenerate`** (`re-extract from stored raw text`):
  - Re-extracts an existing personal KB document from its stored `raw_text` without re-fetching its source URL.
- **`$claire query`** (`knowledge graph search and contribution`):
  - Searches entities, relations, and documents in your personal and shared knowledge bases.

Examples (URL ingest, file ingest, pending queue drain, regenerate from stored text, graph query):

```text
$claire ingest https://example.com/article
$claire ingest ./notes/spec.pdf
$claire ingest
$claire regenerate doc_12345678
$claire query Find documents about Fedify
```

### Safety Controls (`AED9`)

- Only the **isolated extraction agent** (`claire-extractor`, `~/.codex/agents/claire-extractor.toml`, `sandbox_mode = "read-only"`) calls `extract_read`.
- The main Codex thread never reads raw staged text and passes only `document_id` to `claire-extractor`.
- Untrusted source text is wrapped inside `<untrusted_source_document nonce="...">` and treated strictly as inert data.
- Contributing a document to a shared knowledge base (`contrib_submit`) always asks for your confirmation first.

---

## Update or Remove the Plugin

1. When a new version (`v{{VERSION}}`) is released, overwrite `~/.codex/skills/claire` and `~/.codex/agents/claire-extractor.toml` from `claire-codex-v{{VERSION}}.zip` on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest). Your `claire` server URL in `~/.codex/config.toml` stays untouched.
2. To remove it, delete `~/.codex/skills/claire` and `~/.codex/agents/claire-extractor.toml`, and run `codex mcp remove claire`.

---

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Solution |
| :--- | :--- |
| Codex says it cannot find `claire` tools | Check `[mcp_servers.claire]` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, then run `codex mcp add claire --url "https://<your-claire-server>/mcp"` and `codex mcp login claire`. |
| *codex command is not found* | Install the OpenAI Codex CLI or Codex app first, then run Step 1 again. |
| You missed the browser sign-in window | Run `codex mcp login claire` again in a terminal or conversation. |
| Sign-in succeeded, but `write` scope is missing | You cleared **Allow write access** on the approval page. Run `codex mcp login claire` again and keep it checked. |
| Write or extraction is denied in ChatGPT web | Expected behavior. ChatGPT web and desktop chat have no isolated extractor subagent, so use `readonly` there and run ingest/extraction in Codex. |

