## ChatGPT Web & Desktop: Read-Only Connection

ChatGPT web and desktop chat have no isolated extraction subagent (`claire-extractor`), so they support **search (read) only**.

1. In ChatGPT, open **Settings** -> **Connectors** (or **Apps / Advanced settings**) and turn on **Developer Mode**.
2. Click **Create** to add a custom MCP connector:
   - **Name**: `Claire Bible`
   - **Server URL**: `https://<your-claire-server>/mcp`
   - **Authentication**: `OAuth`
3. When the Claire Bible OAuth 2.1 consent page opens, **clear `Allow write access`** and approve. (Only `readonly` is granted, so raw source reads and writes are blocked on the server.)
4. In a new chat, select Developer Mode or the Claire Bible connector and ask, for example, *"Find documents about a topic in Claire Bible"*.

For saving and extracting sources, use Codex set up with Steps 1 and 2 above.

<details>
<summary>Terminal / Manual Setup (.zip, .tar.gz, and SHA256SUMS)</summary>

```bash
curl -LO "https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest/download/claire-codex-v{{VERSION}}.tar.gz"
curl -LO "https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest/download/SHA256SUMS"
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing
mkdir -p ~/.codex/skills ~/.codex/agents
tar -xzf claire-codex-v{{VERSION}}.tar.gz -C /tmp
cp -r /tmp/claire/skills/claire ~/.codex/skills/claire
cp /tmp/claire/agents/claire-extractor.toml ~/.codex/agents/claire-extractor.toml
codex mcp add claire --url "https://<your-claire-server>/mcp"
codex mcp login claire
```

- Inside a Codex session, `/mcp` shows the live connection status of `claire`.

</details>
